Requirements: 4   with obligations: 4

[task-01] Two tests in `tests/test_execution_sandbox.py`,
    `test_a_budget_that_cannot_be_enforced_declines_the_run` and
    `test_the_per_test_budget_still_applies_without_a_report_path`, call the network-
    blocking pytest plugin's `pytest_configure` directly. That installs the network
    block in the test suite's own process and never removes it, so every test that runs
    afterwards finds `socket.create_connection`, `socket.getaddrinfo` and
    `socket.socket.connect` replaced.
    -> call-network-blocking-pytest-configure-directly  [functional/explicit]
       Call the network-blocking pytest plugin's `pytest_configure` directly.
    -> network-block-installed-in-test-process  [functional/explicit]
       The network block is installed in the test suite's own process.
    -> preserve-installed-network-block  [invariant/explicit]
       The network block installed by the pytest plugin remains in place after the
       direct `pytest_configure` call.

[task-02] When the work is done, both tests leave the process's `socket` module as they
    found them: after either test runs, `socket.create_connection`, `socket.getaddrinfo`
    and `socket.socket.connect` are the original functions. Neither test is about the
    network block, so each should skip installing it rather than install and remove it.
    -> socket-module-restored-after-tests  [regression/explicit]
       Both tests leave the process's socket module as they found it, so after either
       test runs, socket.create_connection, socket.getaddrinfo, and
       socket.socket.connect are the original functions.
    -> skip-network-block-installation  [regression/explicit]
       Neither test installs the network block; each test skips installing it instead of
       installing and removing it.
    -> skip-network-block-installation-2  [functional/explicit]
       Each test should skip installing the network block and leave the process's socket
       module untouched by that setup step.

[task-03] This is a reported defect, so a regression test that fails while the block is
    left installed and passes once it is not is part of the deliverable.
    -> regression-test-block-left-installed  [test_demand/explicit]
       A regression test fails while the block is left installed and passes once it is
       not.

[exclusion-01] Changing how the network block itself works for the projects the tool
